.TH TMUX-COPY-LAST-OUTPUT 1 "2026-06-30" "cmdblocks" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tmux-copy-last-output \- copy recent tmux command blocks to the clipboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tmux-copy-last-output
.RI [ count ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tmux-copy-last-output
captures the current tmux pane, detects shell prompt boundaries, and copies the
most recent command plus its output to the clipboard. When
.I count
is supplied, it must be a positive base-10 integer and the command copies that
many recent command blocks. The default is one.
.PP
The parser is tuned for the two-line prompt shape used by the surrounding
terminal setup. If no complete command block is found, the command displays a
tmux message and exits successfully so keybindings do not fail noisily.
.SH CLIPBOARD BACKENDS
The command tries
.BR pbcopy (1)
on macOS,
.BR xclip (1)
when
.B DISPLAY
is set, and finally OSC 52 through the attached tmux client TTY.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command copied output, reported that no block was found, or displayed a
clipboard failure message through tmux.
.TP
.B 1
An unexpected shell, tmux, or parsing failure occurred before tmux messaging
could report the result.
.TP
.B 64
The arguments were invalid. The command writes a usage diagnostic before any
tmux or clipboard command is invoked.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR term-notify-sound (1)
